#!/usr/bin/env bash
# =============================================================================
# oc-deploy — fleet ship/poll/swap script (target-process-20260827.md).
#
# ONE script for the ship -> build -> deploy loop, run as a background task
# from the invoking agent (owner directive 2026-08-27 19:17Z: ship 2+3 and
# poll 8-17 are the SAME script; the agent launches it, the runtime injects
# the result). Replaces compiler dispatch+poll duties per staged plan:
#   S0 inert (plan-only) -> S1 shadow ship (dispatch live, swaps stay
#   compiler) -> S2 pilot swap -> S3 cutover (DONE 2026-08-28: compiler
#   retired; poll = THE deploy path; runbook = tools/archive/compiler.md archived).
#
#   oc-deploy ship [--sha <40-hex>] [--features <set>] [--execute]
#   oc-deploy poll [--execute]
#   oc-deploy swap-execute --sha <40-hex> --run <id> [--features F]
#                          [--artifact-dir D] [--drill]        # Phase B
#   oc-deploy watch [--with-delta]       # stray-commit tripwire (report-only)
#                                        # + optional upstream arithmetic leg
#   oc-deploy contributors <old>..<new> | --deployed [--repo R]   # issue #24 D1
#   oc-deploy fanout --run <id> [--dry-run]   # issue #24: mechanical notify fan-out
#   oc-deploy --selftest
#
# S2 WIRING (2026-08-28, per s2-swap-journal-spec.md + owner tool-logging law):
#   - swap-execute = Phase B body. Runs under a systemd-run --user TRANSIENT
#     unit (spawned by init, not the opencrabs daemon) so the bounce it
#     triggers cannot kill its own verifier. poll --execute at S2 hands off
#     to that unit and exits BEFORE any bounce (Phase A/B split).
#   - JOURNAL: $STATE_DIR/oc-deploy/journal/swap-<short>-<epoch>.jsonl —
#     append-only, one fsync'd JSON line per state-changing step BEFORE the
#     next step starts (auto-swap/backup/verify/install/seal/marker-write/
#     restart/post-verify/receipt/rollback). Last present line = last
#     completed step; a crash is reconstructable from the journal alone.
#   - MARKERS: deployed.sha + deployed.meta.json written by THIS script
#     between seal and restart (the 03:11Z gap: HQ had to hand-restore).
#     Rollback restores markers + baseline/orders backups too.
#   - LEDGER STAMP: every attempt (success OR rollback OR drill) ends with a
#     flock'd workers-ledger stamp kind=swap-result quoting the journal.
#   - AUTO-ROLLBACK: post-bounce verify fail = restore backup + restart +
#     re-verify + stamp ROLLED_BACK + A2A owner ping, automatic.
#   - NO CONSENT GATE (owner 2026-08-28 18:50Z: consent process ELIMINATED):
#     GREEN carrier run + artifact verify IS the authorization -> auto-swap.
#     Post-SMOKE-FAIL rollback stays the owner's call (no auto-rollback there);
#     the swap-chain auto-rollback on post-bounce verify fail is unchanged.
#
# HARD SAFETY RULES (v0.4.27 + S2):
#   - Plan-only UNLESS --execute. Every planned action prints as "PLAN: ...".
#     NEVER bare exit 0 — plan mode always prints its full delta.
#   - Kill file aborts EVERY invocation first (exit 9), selftest included.
#     Either $STATE_DIR/oc-deploy.kill or /root/oc-work/oc-deploy.disabled.
#   - Swap actions (poll execute + swap-execute) require stage >= S2.
#   - Consent gate RETIRED 2026-08-28 (owner order): GREEN run -> auto-swap.
#   - Shadow journal $STATE_DIR/oc-deploy-shadow.log records every run.
#   - Bash-only, seconds of runtime, zero cargo.
#
# Exit codes: 0 ok/noop | 1 usage | 2 rebase/gate/push/verify/rollback fail
#             / watch stray | 3 retired (was consent) | 4 stage gate / launch fail
#             | 9 kill file
# Deps: git, gh, jq, curl; oc-order-validate (ship execute);
#       oc-artifact-verify + oc-seal-state (swap-execute real mode)
# =============================================================================
